id: zw_cc_multi_channel_control
label: Multi Channel Command Class Control
category: Z-Wave|Command Classes
description: >
  The Multi Channel Command Class is used to manage associations to Multi Channel End
  Point destinations as well as to NodeID destinations. An association group sends an unsolicited
  command to the configured destinations when triggered by an event. The parameters of the command
  may be dynamic, e.g. the temperature of a sensor reading or the light level for a dimmer.
package: zwave
quality: production
metadata:
  sbom:
    reference: zw_sbom_license

source:
- path: ZAF/CommandClasses/MultiChan/src/multichannel.c
include:
- path: ZAF/CommandClasses/MultiChan/inc/
  file_list:
  - path: multichannel.h
provides:
- name: zw_cc_multi_channel_control
root_path: zwave
